patterns.evidence:
The global base has fallen every year since 2018, from 3.24m in 2019 to 2.9m in 2024. Western Europe fell -3.6% in 2022 to 352,770 and heads to 316,126 by 2028 (-1.8% CAGR). The euro-area ECB series is -5.7% over 2yr. CEE is flat (RBR 236,507 to 231,895 by 2028, -0.1% CAGR).

The live footprint splits three ways (IAD = independent ATM deployer):
GROWING — Hungary +18.6% (mandate), Greece +15.3% (deployer/IAD wave), Montenegro +23% (2024), Albania +8%, Kosovo +8.4%, Serbia back to +3.6% (Q1'26);
STABLE — Bulgaria, Slovenia, Cyprus, Ukraine (~15.7k held flat through 3 war years);
DECLINING — Austria -4.6%/2yr, Czechia -3.7%.

RBR expects 6 of 12 primary CEE markets to grow to 2028.
